Package: DPprior
Title: Principled Prior Elicitation for Dirichlet Process Mixture Models
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", , "jlee296@ua.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Tools for eliciting Gamma hyperpriors on the concentration
    parameter alpha in Dirichlet Process (DP) mixture models. Rather than
    requiring specification of the abstract parameter alpha directly,
    'DPprior' allows researchers to express prior beliefs through intuitive
    quantities: occupied-cluster counts and named weight estimands. The package
    implements Two-Stage Moment Matching (TSMM) with an explicit closed-form
    proxy (A1), independently verified Newton-based moment matching (A2-MN),
    and distributional calibration (A2-KL). Versioned canonical results retain
    computation, verification, and provenance evidence. Separate hard and soft
    dual-anchor workflows support verified inequalities and fixed-scale
    trade-offs. Based on methods described in Lee (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2602.06301> and Lee, Che, Rabe-Hesketh, Feller, and Miratrix (2025)
    <doi:10.3102/10769986241254286>.
